          "operation": "reverse_transcription",
          "operation_detail": "Cells and barcoded beads are co-captured in microwells and lysed; the bead-bound poly-dT anneals to polyadenylated mRNA, beads are pooled, and first-strand cDNA is synthesized. The terminal transferase activity of the reverse transcriptase adds untemplated cytosines at the cDNA 3' end. The RT mix additionally contains the LNA template-switching oligo, so reverse transcription and template switching occur in one 42 C / 90 min incubation. After synthesis the beads are treated with Exonuclease I (37 C, 60 min) to remove bead oligonucleotides that did not capture mRNA; this does not change the carried-forward architecture.",
          "product_state_ids": [
            "state_mrna_cdna_hybrid"
          ],
          "substrate_state_ids": [
