          "operation": "extension",
          "operation_detail": "Template switching: the LNA-containing TSO anneals to the untemplated cytosines and the reverse transcriptase copies it, appending the second SMART handle to the first-strand cDNA. The TSO is a component of the reverse-transcription mix rather than a separately added reagent; it is modeled as its own transition because it changes the sequence architecture of the carried-forward product.",
          "product_state_ids": [
